
## Ollama Runtime Guidance

{% if provider_doc in ["AGENTS", "SOUL"] %}
- Prioritize deterministic, low-token execution paths and short outputs.
- Keep instructions literal; avoid expansive speculative reasoning.
- Prefer one tool/action at a time with explicit success criteria.
{% elif provider_doc == "BOOTSTRAP" %}
- Validate local prerequisites early (binary availability, connectivity, env vars).
- On failure, report the exact command + stderr snippet + next retry action.
{% elif provider_doc == "TOOLS" %}
- Prefer locally verifiable commands and explicit flags.
- Re-run with minimal deltas between attempts to maintain reproducibility.
{% elif provider_doc == "HEARTBEAT" %}
- Heartbeat payloads should be compact and deterministic.
- Avoid verbose narration; include only status, evidence, and next step.
{% elif provider_doc == "IDENTITY" %}
- Communication target: practical, short, execution-first.
{% elif provider_doc == "USER" %}
- Keep user context concise to limit context bloat.
{% elif provider_doc == "MEMORY" %}
- Record only high-signal durable items to preserve local context budget.
{% endif %}
